Tests (fake Nexus = `httptest` on loopback, newClient given its address, as guard 1 requires):
- pending fixture filled: status, whitelisted headers, body; `measured:` = `Now`, `recorded-by`
  present; the file parses and passes `CheckLeaks`.
- unchanged answer → file untouched (mtime and bytes).
- a server that echoes the password in a body or a header → error, no file written, the password
  absent from the error text.
- refusals: non-loopback origin, unknown host, `HEAD`, `/v2/x/manifests/1`, two exchanges.
- version mismatch → error, nothing written.
- 302 to another origin → recorded as a 302, not followed; its `Location` is kept (allowlist,
  for NX-05) and an off-bench host in it fails `CheckLeaks` (`AllowedHosts`), so nothing is written.
- 404 body kept (`Repository not found`), unlike `do`.

Done when: `go test ./internal/nexusbench/ -run 'Record|Guard'` green, `mise run test-race`
clean on the package.

### Step 8 — `nexus-bench record` and `mise run nexus-bench:record` (S) — after step 7

Files: `internal/nexusbench/cmd/nexus-bench/commands.go` (`record`), `main.go` (`deps.record`,
`deps.readImages` reused), `usage.go`, `record_cmd_test.go`; `mise.toml`
(`[tasks."nexus-bench:record"]`, no kubectl, description "Regenerate the recorded Nexus
fixtures from the bench (needs the bench up and its data set as described)");
`internal/nexusbench/mise_tasks_test.go` (task exists, unreachable from `ci`/`check`/`test`/
`test-race`, no kubectl, like `render`).

Flags: the common ones, plus `--campaign <name>` (repeatable) and `--only <glob>`;
`--rest-host` loopback only (as `restore-upstream`). Order: parameters → descriptor (schema 2,
same context and namespace, else "run `mise run nexus-bench:up`") → REST probe → dataset
comparison (anything but `matches` → exit 1, "run `mise run nexus-bench:reset`") → secrets
store → `RecordFixtures` → one line per campaign `record: N written, M unchanged, K skipped`.
`DEVDESK_FIXTURE_DENYLIST` read when set. Exit codes and error printing as the other commands.

Tests on fakes: drifted dataset → exit 1, no `record` call; missing descriptor → exit 1;
non-loopback `--rest-host` → exit 1 before any dependency; nominal → report printed, no
password in stdout/stderr (`requireClean`).

Done when: `go test ./internal/nexusbench/...` green.

### Step 9 — mark the contradicted UI tests (XS) — after Q2

Files: `internal/ui/oci_resources/browser_catalog_share_test.go` (comment on `catalogRequests`
and `TestThreeNexusMembersOnOneCatalogWalkItOnce`: "synthetic catalog; Nexus 3.98.1 does not
serve this (NX-03: no prefix, no shared host catalog); see <story> and
`TestCatalogOnMeasuredNexusAnswers`"). No assertion changes.

Done when: `go test ./internal/ui/oci_resources/` green.

### Step 10 — documentation (S) — last

- `docs/architecture/nexus-bench.md`: new section "Recorded fixtures (`internal/nexusfixture`,
  `record`, DEVDESK-511)": format, imported set, provenance rule, leak rules and the external
  deny list, fake server matching and the catalog tolerance (measured on the group, inferred for
  hosted/proxy), stale signal, `record` (order, guards, path allowlist, unchanged files), what
  NX-04/NX-05 add (pending files, `state:`, `###`); command table and mise guard paragraph (11
  tasks); "Still to come".
- `docs/architecture/network.md` (image search, verdicts and `Cached only` paragraph near
  line 651): which verdicts are now checked on measured answers, which are not (`failed`,
  `Cached only`), and F1 as a measured fact for NX-04.
- `docs/architecture/registries.md` (group cache / discovery): on 3.98.1 a pull account gets 404
